A partial: the compliance-lens gate. D-SETTINGS-LINE: it imports nothing from
`_settings.mds`. Its host expands the settings block once, before the earliest of
its consumers, and the lens is set from the line resolved there for the
worktree's root.

D-COMPLIANCE-INJECT: the compliance instruction reaches an agent only through a spawn
prompt, and only when the resolved lens is on. No Code, Fix, Review or Design body names
the compliance skill, so a lens-off spawn pays nothing for it. `compliance_directive()` is the
one home of the directive text; `compliance_inject()` is how a pass-through host sets it.
No install-time variant carries the lens: it is the union of the machine, the default
branch and the worktree (D-LENS-UNION), so a repository can turn it on when the machine
switch is off. The posting steps are the opposite case. They are an install-time variant
keyed on the machine switch alone, as compliance arms in each host, and a repository key
cannot restore one.

@define compliance_frameworks():
`COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS` is the settings line's `COMPLIANCE` with `generic` written `none`: `off`, `none`, or the framework ids the machine and this repository declare.
@end

@define compliance_lens():
**Resolve the compliance lens** for each worktree root, from its settings line — the line resolved above for that root, by the settings block when this run has not yet resolved it (every framework reference is installed on every machine, so no file check decides it).

**Set the compliance lens** from that line: {{compliance_frameworks()}}
@end

@define compliance_gate():
{{compliance_lens()}}

`COMPLIANCE_ACTIVE` is `true` unless `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS` is `off`.
@end

@define compliance_load(ids):
invoke Skill(skill="devflow:compliance") and load references/{id}.md only for the ids in {{ids}} (none: generic controls only); never fabricate guidance for a framework you were not given.
@end

@define compliance_directive(ids):
When the task touches regulated surface (data models, auth flows, logging/observability, payments, IaC, retention), {{compliance_load(ids)}}
@end

@define compliance_focus_directive(ids):
For this compliance focus, {{compliance_load(ids)}}
@end

@define compliance_inject():
**Set the compliance directive** from `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS`. `COMPLIANCE_DIRECTIVE` is empty when `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS` is `off`: a spawn line that holds only `{COMPLIANCE_DIRECTIVE}` is then left out, so a lens-off spawn carries nothing about compliance. Otherwise `COMPLIANCE_DIRECTIVE` is this one line, with `<ids>` replaced by the value of `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS`:

> {{compliance_directive("<ids>")}}
@end

@define compliance_focus_inject():
**Set the compliance focus directive** from `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS`. `COMPLIANCE_FOCUS_DIRECTIVE` is this one line, with `<ids>` replaced by the value of `COMPLIANCE_FRAMEWORKS`; only the compliance focus's spawn carries it:

> {{compliance_focus_directive("<ids>")}}
@end

@export compliance_frameworks
@export compliance_lens
@export compliance_gate
@export compliance_directive
@export compliance_focus_directive
@export compliance_inject
@export compliance_focus_inject
